  "notes": "USAGE:\nPrimarily used as a suru verb: {結成|けっせい}する (to form, to organize). Used for deliberate, purposeful creation of groups — bands, political parties, committees, teams, alliances.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- バンドを{結成|けっせい}する: to form a band\n- {政党|せいとう}を{結成|けっせい}する: to form a political party\n- チームを{結成|けっせい}する: to form a team\n- {同盟|どうめい}を{結成|けっせい}する: to form an alliance\n- {委員会|いいんかい}を{結成|けっせい}する: to form a committee\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{設立|せつりつ} (establishment) is used for more formal organizations like companies and institutions. {結成|けっせい} implies people coming together voluntarily for a shared cause.",
